  "body": "The maintainer asked for this work in chat on 2026-11-15: \"revieww AGENTS.md and compress its meaning into something more useful, use the ASDSTE-100 standard, move functionality out of Agents and into Skills if it makes sense.\" The reason he gave earlier: \"Its eating way to much of your token capacity\".\n\nWhat happens: `AGENTS.md` on main has 1240 lines (81 kB). Each session loads all of it. Most of the text is procedure for one task (a release cut, a fork sync, a runner installation) or history (dated quotations, superseded rules).\n\nExpected:\n\n- `AGENTS.md` keeps each rule, in ASD-STE100, without the history.\n- A procedure that only one task uses moves into a skill in `.claude/skills/`. A session loads it only for that task.\n- No rule changes its meaning. The rule names that skills and agents cite stay the same.\n\nDone means: the PR shows the size before and after, lists where each moved section is now, and the maintainer accepts that no rule is lost.\n",
